<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said on Tuesday it allocated 2.46 billion guilders to the money market under a three-day special advances pact at an unchanged rate of 2.50 percent.</p>
<p>Individual banks' applications up to 3.50 billion guilders were met for 13 percent. Above that level, no subscriptions were awarded.</p>
<p>The pact replaces a seven-day facility of 2.11 billion guilders, which expired today.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsdesk +31 20 504 5000</p>
